.TH smi-pki-generate-private-key "1" "September 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI PKI Command"
.SH NAME
smi-pki-generate-private-key \- Generate an RSA private key into a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-pki-generate-private-key
.I OUT_KEY_FILE
.RI [ BITS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Generates an RSA private key into \fIOUT_KEY_FILE\fR. \fIBITS\fR defaults to 2048; CA keys use 4096.
It is a thin command line wrapper over the matching function in the file based PKI library
\fBpki.sh\fR, so each step of building a CA and signing certificates can be run and inspected
on its own. All material is passed as file names; the command fails if the underlying OpenSSL
operation fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smi-pki-ca-create (1),
.BR smi-pki-create-domain-cert (1),
.BR openssl (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Imre Tabur <imre.tabur@mail.ee>
